Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/aix5ppc-core.c
Line: 307
Function: xcoff64_core_file_matches_executable_p
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: After growing the path buffer, the code adjusts the write pointer incorrectly: s = n + (path - s) instead of s = n + (s - path). This moves s before the start of the newly allocated buffer. Subsequent bfd_read(s, 1, ...) writes a byte before the heap buffer, causing heap memory corruption. This is reachable when the path read from the core is at least 100 bytes long, triggering the reallocation.

